      "lineNbr": 888,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-15T17:40:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `blueprint:\"mutated\"` tag means that it cannot be specified in an Android.bp file but is modified at runtime. As it is a property it means that just like all other properties they are copied into a new variants created of the module.\n\nIf you want to be able to specify the property in an Android.bp file then you will have to remove the `blueprint:\"mutated\"` tag from it.\n\nI was suggesting that you add a separate property, say something like this:\n\n    EnforceDefaultTargetSdkVersion bool `blueprint:\"mutated\"`\n    \nAnd then set that based on the value of Updatable and Enforce_default_target_sdk_version instead of modifying Enforce_default_target_sdk_version. Similar to how the java.CommonProperties.Instrument property is handled.\n\nModifying Enforce_default_target_sdk_version loses information as you cannot determine whether it was specified in an Android.bp file.",
      "parentUuid": "a6d8026d_211d56d1",
      "revId": "e15a971aa6078756890df7a22135c4f9de1ef9d9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
